#
# Counter-example for math:IntervalKindConflationShape (Rule I3): ONE node typed BOTH
# math:ConfidenceInterval AND math:CredibleInterval — frequentist coverage under a
# sampling procedure conflated with Bayesian posterior mass. They are held owl:disjointWith
# THROUGH their paradigm parents (math:ConfidenceInterval ⊑ math:FrequentistResult,
# math:CredibleInterval ⊑ math:BayesianResult, math:FrequentistResult owl:disjointWith
# math:BayesianResult), so the sh:not [ sh:class math:CredibleInterval ] fires —
# shacl.NotConstraintComponent (math:IntervalKindConflation).
# Single violation: the node is COMPLETE for BOTH kinds — its two bounds and framed
# math:confidenceLevel satisfy math:IncompleteConfidenceIntervalShape (Rule I4), and its
# math:hasPosterior and framed math:credibleMass satisfy math:IncompleteCredibleIntervalShape
# (Rule I5) — so ONLY the sh:not fires, EXACTLY ONE finding, no completeness sibling.
# Back-reference: math:IntervalKindConflation (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Negative counterpart of conformance-fixtures/interval-kinds-distinct.ttl.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecIntervalKindConflation).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

# One node typed BOTH interval kinds, complete for each so only the conflation fires.
ex:conflatedInterval a math:ConfidenceInterval , math:CredibleInterval ;
    math:hasIntervalBound ex:loBound , ex:hiBound ;
    math:confidenceLevel ex:ciLevel ;      # completes the confidence-interval frame
    math:hasPosterior ex:paramPosterior ;  # completes the credible-interval posterior
    math:credibleMass ex:credMass .        # completes the credible-interval mass

ex:loBound a math:MathematicalObject .
ex:hiBound a math:MathematicalObject .

ex:ciLevel a math:ProbabilityValue , math:RationalValue ;
    math:numerator 95 ;        # 95/100 = 0.95, within [0, 1]
    math:denominator 100 ;
    gmeow:hasReferenceFrame ex:samplingFrame .

ex:samplingFrame a gmeow:ReferenceFrame .

ex:paramPosterior a math:PosteriorDistribution ;
    math:distributionFamily ex:betaFamily .

ex:betaFamily a math:DistributionFamily .

ex:credMass a math:ProbabilityValue , math:RationalValue ;
    math:numerator 95 ;        # 95/100 = 0.95, within [0, 1]
    math:denominator 100 ;
    gmeow:hasReferenceFrame ex:posteriorFrame .

ex:posteriorFrame a gmeow:ReferenceFrame .
<http://example.org/math/ciLevel> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
<http://example.org/math/credMass> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
